{{fbdoc item="title" value="__CMDLINE__"}}----
Intrinsic define (macro value) set by the compiler

{{fbdoc item="syntax"}}##
	""__CMDLINE__""
##
{{fbdoc item="desc"}}
	##""__CMDLINE__""## is a string literal containing the option text from accepted source ###cmdline## directives in the current compilation. The directive text is joined in source order with one space between directives.

	It reflects options supplied by source directives, not the arguments used to launch **fbc**. It is an empty string when no non-empty source ###cmdline## options have been accepted.

{{fbdoc item="ver"}}
	- Since fbc 1.20.4

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}
%%(freebasic)
#cmdline "-v"
#cmdline "-s gui"

#print __CMDLINE__ ' -v -s gui
%%

{{fbdoc item="see"}}
	- ##[[KeyPgPpcmdline|#cmdline]]##
	- ##[[KeyPgDdfbverbose|__FB_VERBOSE__]]##

{{fbdoc item="back" value="CatPgDddefines|Intrinsic Defines"}}
